{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/720", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Create a completely fictional alien race that follow the following list of requirements.\\n\\nRequirements:\\n1. They must have a name that seems unpronounceable to the human mind\\n2. You must provide a physical description of the alien race\\n3. You must provide a description of the capabilities, including but not limited to: Their scientific advancements, military capabilities, and healthcare, whether it be good or bad\\n4. What alien religion do they follow?\", \"response\": \"Name: The alien race is called the \\\"Xh'k't'l'la'n\\\"\\n\\nPhysical Description: The Xh'k't'l'la'n are a tall, thin race with elongated limbs and a flexible, rubbery exoskeleton. They have multiple sets of eyes, which are arranged in a circular pattern around their head, giving them a 360-degree field of vision. They have a unique respiratory system that allows them to breathe in the toxic atmosphere of their home planet.\\n\\nCapabilities: The Xh'k't'l'la'n are a highly advanced race with a strong focus on science and technology. They have developed advanced propulsion systems that allow them to travel faster than the speed of light, and they have also made significant advancements in biotechnology and genetic engineering. Their military is highly advanced, with powerful weapons and advanced shielding technology. They have a highly advanced healthcare system that is able to cure most diseases and extend life expectancy well beyond what is possible on Earth.\\n\\nReligion: The Xh'k't'l'la'n follow a religion based on the worship of a deity they call the \\\"Great Symbiote.\\\" They believe that all life in the universe is interconnected and that the Great Symbiote is the source of this interconnectedness. They believe that by living in harmony with the universe and with each other, they can achieve a state of spiritual enlightenment and become one with the Great Symbiote.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/399", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain this:\\n\\nRun-time Structure\\nLanguages can be classified in several\\ncategories, according to their execution-time\\nstructure.\\n1)Static languages\\n2)Stack-based languages\\n3)Dynamic languages\", \"response\": \"Here are the three main categories of programming languages based on their run-time structure:\\n\\n1. Static languages: These languages use static type checking, which means that the type of each variable and expression is checked at compile time. The compiler verifies that all types are compatible and that operations are valid. Examples of static languages include C, C++, Java, and Python.\\n\\n2. Stack-based languages: These languages use a stack-based memory model, where variables are stored on a stack and accessed in a last-in, first-out (LIFO) manner. The stack is a fixed-size memory area that grows and shrinks as variables are pushed and popped. Examples of stack-based languages include assembly language, Lisp, and Perl.\\n\\n3. Dynamic languages: These languages use dynamic type checking, which means that the type of each variable and expression is checked at run time. The interpreter or runtime system verifies that all types are compatible and that operations are valid. Examples of dynamic languages include JavaScript, Ruby, and PHP.\\n\\nIn dynamic languages, the type of a variable can change during the course of a program's execution, whereas in static languages, the type of a variable is fixed at compile time. Stack-based languages use a different memory model than dynamic or static languages, and they have their own advantages and disadvantages.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
